<title>RUSSIA: Russia eases repo rules for primary dealers.</title>
<headline>Russia eases repo rules for primary dealers.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Central Bank said on Wednesday it was easing rules for conducting repos for primary dealers in the government securities market.</p>
<p>From February 20 primary dealers will be able to conduct repo agreements for any purpose, and not simply to close short positions arising from trading T-bills and government bonds with the Central Bank, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Repos were started in October, allowing banks to run up a two-day overdraft with the Central Bank when buying government securities.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
